{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SeyEDvtMRM3VFBXaH8vLVh","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd067-split\n2\ttitle: \"cmd/split: Split a File into Pieces\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  Shell scripts and data pipelines use split to divide large files into smaller pieces by\n6\t  line count, byte count, or number of chunks. The macOS BSD split differs from GNU split\n7\t  in suffix handling, numeric suffixes, and additional splitting modes. The Go implementation\n8\t  must match the Homebrew GNU reference binary (gsplit, installed by coreutils) in output\n9\t  and exit codes for all supported flag combinations, verified by differential testing via\n10\t  pkg/testutils.\n11\t\n12\tgoals:\n13\t  - G1: Split a file into pieces by line count (default mode).\n14\t  - G2: Split a file by byte count or into a fixed number of chunks.\n15\t  - G3: Support configurable output prefix and suffix options.\n16\t  - G4: Verify functional parity against gsplit via differential testing.\n17\t\n18\trequirements:\n19\t  R1:\n20\t    title: Default behavior and line-based splitting\n21\t    items:\n22\t      - R1.1:\n23\t          text: When invoked with no options, must split the input into pieces of 1000 lines each, writing to files named xaa, xab, xac, etc.\n24\t      - R1.2:\n25\t          text: \"When a PREFIX argument is given, must use PREFIX instead of 'x' as the output filename prefix.\"\n26\t      - R1.3:\n27\t          text: \"-l N or --lines=N must split the input into pieces of N lines each.\"\n28\t      - R1.4:\n29\t          text: When reading from stdin or when FILE is \"-\", must read from stdin.\n30\t\n31\t  R2:\n32\t    title: Byte-based and chunk-based splitting\n33\t    items:\n34\t      - R2.1:\n35\t          text: \"-b N or --bytes=N must split the input into pieces of N bytes each. N may have a suffix (K, M, G, T, P, E, Z, Y for powers of 1024, or KB, MB, etc. for powers of 1000).\"\n36\t      - R2.2:\n37\t          text: \"-C N or --line-bytes=N must split the input into pieces of at most N bytes each, breaking only at line boundaries. Lines longer than N bytes are written to their own piece.\"\n38\t      - R2.3:\n39\t          text: \"-n CHUNKS or --number=CHUNKS must split the input into CHUNKS pieces of roughly equal size. Must support N (by bytes), l/N (by lines), and r/N (round-robin by lines) forms.\"\n40\t      - R2.4:\n41\t          text: \"Must not split in more than one mode simultaneously; conflicting split options must produce an error and exit 1.\"\n42\t\n43\t  R3:\n44\t    title: Suffix control and additional options\n45\t    items:\n46\t      - R3.1:\n47\t          text: \"-a N or --suffix-length=N must use suffixes of length N (default 2).\"\n48\t      - R3.2:\n49\t          text: \"-d or --numeric-suffixes must use numeric suffixes (00, 01, 02, ...) instead of alphabetic.\"\n50\t      - R3.3:\n51\t          text: \"--additional-suffix=SUFFIX must append SUFFIX to each output filename after the alphabetic or numeric suffix.\"\n52\t      - R3.4:\n53\t          text: \"--filter=COMMAND must write each piece to the given shell COMMAND via a pipe, with the output filename available as $FILE in the command.\"\n54\t\n55\t  R4:\n56\t    title: Exit codes and differential testing\n57\t    items:\n58\t      - R4.1:\n59\t          text: Must exit 0 when the input is split successfully.\n60\t      - R4.2:\n61\t          text: Must exit 1 when an invalid option, conflicting options, or write error occurs.\n62\t      - R4.3:\n63\t          text: \"Differential tests must compare output file contents and exit codes between the Go binary and the reference binary via pkg/testutils.\"\n64\t      - R4.4:\n65\t          text: \"Tests must cover: default 1000-line split, -l with custom line count, -b byte split with and without suffixes, -C line-bytes, -n chunk modes, -a suffix length, -d numeric suffixes, --additional-suffix, stdin input, custom prefix, and error cases (conflicting options, invalid counts).\"\n66\t\n67\tnon_goals:\n68\t  - cmd/split does not implement --verbose output mode.\n69\t  - cmd/split does not implement --elide-empty-files beyond what -n provides natively.\n70\t\n71\tpackage_contract:\n72\t  imports:\n73\t    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sizeparse\n74\t    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\n75\t\n76\tacceptance_criteria:\n77\t  - id: AC1\n78\t    criterion: \"seq 1 3000 | go run ./cmd/split produces xaa (lines 1-1000), xab (lines 1001-2000), xac (lines 2001-3000), matching gsplit.\"\n79\t    traces:\n80\t      - R1.1\n81\t      - R1.3\n82\t      - R1.4\n83\t  - id: AC2\n84\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/split -b 100 testfile produces pieces of 100 bytes each, matching gsplit.\"\n85\t    traces:\n86\t      - R2.1\n87\t      - R4.1\n88\t  - id: AC3\n89\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/split -d -a 3 testfile chunk_ produces chunk_000, chunk_001, etc., matching gsplit.\"\n90\t    traces:\n91\t      - R1.2\n92\t      - R3.1\n93\t      - R3.2\n94\t  - id: AC4\n95\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/split -n 3 testfile produces 3 roughly equal pieces, matching gsplit.\"\n96\t    traces:\n97\t      - R2.3\n98\t  - id: AC5\n99\t    criterion: \"Differential test against gsplit passes for all flag combinations listed in R4.4.\"\n100\t    traces:\n101\t      - R4.3\n102\t      - R4.4\n103\t  - id: AC6\n104\t    criterion: \"cmd/split compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n105\t    traces:\n106\t      - R1.1\n107\t      - R1.2\n108\t      - R1.3\n109\t      - R1.4\n110\t      - R2.1\n111\t      - R2.2\n112\t      - R2.3\n113\t      - R2.4\n114\t      - R3.1\n115\t      - R3.2\n116\t      - R3.3\n117\t      - R3.4\n118\t      - R4.1\n119\t      - R4.2\n120\t      - R4.3\n121\t      - R4.4\n122\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"712b3c0a-6d67-4325-96d0-05fbcefa3c92","uuid":"826a3803-d5b4-4a24-904d-c228472c1949","timestamp":"2026-05-21T19:09:33.643Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5444/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd067-split.yaml","content":"id: srd067-split\ntitle: \"cmd/split: Split a File into Pieces\"\n\nproblem: |\n  Shell scripts and data pipelines use split to divide large files into smaller pieces by\n  line count, byte count, or number of chunks. The macOS BSD split differs from GNU split\n  in suffix handling, numeric suffixes, and additional splitting modes. The Go implementation\n  must match the Homebrew GNU reference binary (gsplit, installed by coreutils) in output\n  and exit codes for all supported flag combinations, verified by differential testing via\n  pkg/testutils.\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Split a file into pieces by line count (default mode).\n  - G2: Split a file by byte count or into a fixed number of chunks.\n  - G3: Support configurable output prefix and suffix options.\n  - G4: Verify functional parity against gsplit via differential testing.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: Default behavior and line-based splitting\n    items:\n      - R1.1:\n          text: When invoked with no options, must split the input into pieces of 1000 lines each, writing to files named xaa, xab, xac, etc.\n      - R1.2:\n          text: \"When a PREFIX argument is given, must use PREFIX instead of 'x' as the output filename prefix.\"\n      - R1.3:\n          text: \"-l N or --lines=N must split the input into pieces of N lines each.\"\n      - R1.4:\n          text: When reading from stdin or when FILE is \"-\", must read from stdin.\n\n  R2:\n    title: Byte-based and chunk-based splitting\n    items:\n      - R2.1:\n          text: \"-b N or --bytes=N must split the input into pieces of N bytes each. N may have a suffix (K, M, G, T, P, E, Z, Y for powers of 1024, or KB, MB, etc. for powers of 1000).\"\n      - R2.2:\n          text: \"-C N or --line-bytes=N must split the input into pieces of at most N bytes each, breaking only at line boundaries. Lines longer than N bytes are written to their own piece.\"\n      - R2.3:\n          text: \"-n CHUNKS or --number=CHUNKS must split the input into CHUNKS pieces of roughly equal size. Must support N (by bytes), l/N (by lines), and r/N (round-robin by lines) forms.\"\n      - R2.4:\n          text: \"Must not split in more than one mode simultaneously; conflicting split options must produce an error and exit 1.\"\n\n  R3:\n    title: Suffix control and additional options\n    items:\n      - R3.1:\n          text: \"-a N or --suffix-length=N must use suffixes of length N (default 2).\"\n      - R3.2:\n          text: \"-d or --numeric-suffixes must use numeric suffixes (00, 01, 02, ...) instead of alphabetic.\"\n      - R3.3:\n          text: \"--additional-suffix=SUFFIX must append SUFFIX to each output filename after the alphabetic or numeric suffix.\"\n      - R3.4:\n          text: \"--filter=COMMAND must write each piece to the given shell COMMAND via a pipe, with the output filename available as $FILE in the command.\"\n\n  R4:\n    title: Exit codes and differential testing\n    items:\n      - R4.1:\n          text: Must exit 0 when the input is split successfully.\n      - R4.2:\n          text: Must exit 1 when an invalid option, conflicting options, or write error occurs.\n      - R4.3:\n          text: \"Differential tests must compare output file contents and exit codes between the Go binary and the reference binary via pkg/testutils.\"\n      - R4.4:\n          text: \"Tests must cover: default 1000-line split, -l with custom line count, -b byte split with and without suffixes, -C line-bytes, -n chunk modes, -a suffix length, -d numeric suffixes, --additional-suffix, stdin input, custom prefix, and error cases (conflicting options, invalid counts).\"\n\nnon_goals:\n  - cmd/split does not implement --verbose output mode.\n  - cmd/split does not implement --elide-empty-files beyond what -n provides natively.\n\npackage_contract:\n  imports:\n    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sizeparse\n    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    criterion: \"seq 1 3000 | go run ./cmd/split produces xaa (lines 1-1000), xab (lines 1001-2000), xac (lines 2001-3000), matching gsplit.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n  - id: AC2\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/split -b 100 testfile produces pieces of 100 bytes each, matching gsplit.\"\n    traces:\n      - R2.1\n      - R4.1\n  - id: AC3\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/split -d -a 3 testfile chunk_ produces chunk_000, chunk_001, etc., matching gsplit.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.2\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n  - id: AC4\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/split -n 3 testfile produces 3 roughly equal pieces, matching gsplit.\"\n    traces:\n      - R2.3\n  - id: AC5\n    criterion: \"Differential test against gsplit passes for all flag combinations listed in R4.4.\"\n    traces:\n      - R4.3\n      - R4.4\n  - id: AC6\n    criterion: \"cmd/split compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n      - R2.4\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n      - R3.3\n      - R3.4\n      - R4.1\n      - R4.2\n      - R4.3\n      - R4.4\n","numLines":122,"startLine":1,"totalLines":122}}}
