{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (cobbler orchestrator) issued stitch task #5444 to implement `cmd/split` requirements R1.1-R1.4 from srd067-split. This is the first task for cmd/split — only the default behavior and line-based splitting group (R1) should be implemented. Later tasks will add R2 (byte/chunk splitting), R3 (suffix control), and R4 (exit codes/testing) groups. The deliverables are two new files: `cmd/split/main.go` and `cmd/split/split_test.go`.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - **srd067-split R1.1**: Default split into 1000-line pieces, output files named xaa, xab, xac, etc.\n   - **srd067-split R1.2**: Custom PREFIX argument replaces default 'x' prefix\n   - **srd067-split R1.3**: `-l N` or `--lines=N` flag for custom line count per piece\n   - **srd067-split R1.4**: Read from stdin when FILE is \"-\" or omitted\n   - **Alphabetic suffix generation**: aa, ab, ..., az, ba, bb, ..., zz (2-char default)\n   - **Differential testing pattern**: BuildBinary + RunDiffTests against `gsplit` reference\n   - **SIGPIPE handling**: `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` at start of main()\n   - **pkg/testutils**: DiffTest struct with Name, Args, Stdin, Env, WorkDir, ExitCode, Normalize, ExpectedFiles\n   - **pkg/sys**: InstallSIGPIPEHandler() for SIGPIPE handling\n   - **No git commands**: Git managed externally by orchestrator\n   - **Function size limit**: 40 lines max per function (hard limit from execution constitution)\n   - **File size limit**: 500 lines per Go source file\n   - **Copyright header required**: `// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.` + `// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT`\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **docs/specs/software-requirements/srd067-split.yaml** (READ)\n     - Full SRD for split utility, needed to understand R1.1-R1.4 requirements\n     - R1.1: No options → split into 1000-line pieces, files xaa, xab, xac...\n     - R1.2: PREFIX arg replaces 'x'\n     - R1.3: -l N / --lines=N for custom line count\n     - R1.4: stdin when FILE is \"-\" or omitted\n     - Non-goals: no --verbose, no --elide-empty-files beyond -n\n     - Package imports: pkg/sizeparse, pkg/sys\n   \n   - **pkg/testutils/difftest.go** (PROVIDED in context)\n     - DiffTest struct and RunDiffTests function for differential testing\n     - Key: `type DiffTest struct { Name, Args, Stdin, Env, WorkDir, ExitCode, Normalize, ExpectedFiles }`\n   \n   - **pkg/testutils/build.go** (PROVIDED in context)\n     - `BuildBinary(t, \".\")` compiles cmd/ package and returns binary path\n   \n   - **pkg/sys/sigpipe.go** (PROVIDED in context)\n     - `InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` for SIGPIPE handling\n\n   - **cmd/split/main.go** (TO CREATE)\n     - Entry point for split utility implementing R1.1-R1.4 only\n   \n   - **cmd/split/split_test.go** (TO CREATE)\n     - Differential tests against gsplit for R1.1-R1.4\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet. Only one tool call was made (reading the SRD).\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Read the SRD to understand the full requirement scope for R1.1-R1.4\n   - Identified that only line-based splitting is in scope (no byte/chunk modes)\n   - Identified the alphabetic suffix generation pattern (aa-zz with default length 2)\n   - Noted that flags for R2/R3 should NOT be implemented yet, but the code structure should allow later extension (D4: \"Later tasks will add R2-R4 groups by modifying these files\")\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - Message 1: Massive stitch task prompt with full project context, task description for implementing cmd/split R1.1-R1.4, execution constitution, coding standards, constraints, and acceptance criteria\n   - Message 2: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" — Request to create a detailed summary of the conversation\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Create `cmd/split/main.go` implementing R1.1-R1.4 (line-based splitting, default 1000 lines, custom prefix, -l flag, stdin support)\n   - Create `cmd/split/split_test.go` with differential tests against gsplit\n   - Verify compilation: `go build -o bin/split ./cmd/split/`\n   - Verify tests pass: `go test ./cmd/split/... -count=1`\n   - Verify go vet: `go vet ./cmd/split/...`\n   - Ensure each of R1.1, R1.2, R1.3, R1.4 has at least one differential test case\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading the SRD file (`docs/specs/software-requirements/srd067-split.yaml`) and was about to begin implementing the two files. The SRD reading confirmed:\n   - R1.1: Default 1000-line split with xaa/xab/xac naming\n   - R1.2: PREFIX positional argument\n   - R1.3: -l N / --lines=N flag\n   - R1.4: Stdin when FILE is \"-\" or omitted\n   \n   I had not yet written any code. The implementation plan would be:\n   1. Write cmd/split/main.go with flag parsing (-l/--lines), positional arg parsing (FILE, PREFIX), line-based splitting logic, alphabetic suffix generation\n   2. Write cmd/split/split_test.go with differential tests covering all four requirements\n   3. Build and test\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Write `cmd/split/main.go` and `cmd/split/split_test.go` implementing R1.1-R1.4 per the task description. The task states: \"This is the first task for cmd/split. Only implement requirements R1.1-R1.4. Later tasks will add R2-R4 groups by modifying these files.\" The implementation needs:\n   - main() with sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler(), flag parsing for -l/--lines, positional args for [FILE [PREFIX]]\n   - Line-based splitting writing to PREFIX+suffix files (default prefix \"x\", default suffix length 2, alphabetic)\n   - Stdin support when no FILE or FILE is \"-\"\n   - Differential tests against gsplit covering default split, custom line count, custom prefix, and stdin input\n\nIf you need specific details from befo